    "Source": "\n\/*\r\n    Author or source: Johny Dupej\r\n    \n    This function adds a low-passed signal to the original signal. The low-pass has a quite wide response.\n*\/\r\n\nfloat saturate(float x) {\r\n    return fmin(fmax(-1.0,x),1.0);\r\n}\r\n\nformula_main {\r\n    float selectivity = 70 + KNOB_1 * 140;\r\n    float gain2 = 1 + KNOB_2;\r\n    float ratio = KNOB_3;\r\n    \r\n    float gain1 = 1.0\/(selectivity + 1.0);\r\n\r\n    float cap= (input + cap*selectivity )*gain1;\r\n    float sample = saturate((input + cap*ratio)*gain2);\r\n\r\n    return sample;\n}\n",
